/usr/bin/bash -lc "cat > /tmp/codex-pr-498-review.md <<'EOF'
MUST-FIX

1. "'`getBudget()` fails open on any read/parse/validation error and returns `null`, which makes `checkBudget()` allow task starts and makes `incrementBudget()` / `resetBudget()` silently no-op when `budget.json` is malformed or unreadable. That effectively disables enforcement by corruption/error, while `ac-no-budget` only describes the missing-file case (`src/sessions/store.ts:1603`). Narrow this to the explicit opt-in case (`ENOENT`, and possibly missing session path if intentionally equivalent) and surface malformed/unreadable budget files as errors.

SHOULD-FIX

1. The new tests intentionally assert that corrupt/invalid `budget.json` is treated as "no budget" (`tests/session-budget.test.ts:203`, `tests/session-budget.test.ts:212`). Once the helper is fixed to fail closed on malformed/unreadable budget files, these expectations should be inverted so the tests protect enforcement instead of bypassing it.

Notes

- Requested budget AC coverage is present in `tests/session-budget.test.ts` for `@session-creation-and-env-injection` (`ac-budget`, `ac-budget-local`) and `@task-budget-enforcement` (`ac-atomic-write`, `ac-no-budget`, `ac-no-session`, `ac-block-start`, `ac-increment`, `ac-reset`).
- `kspec validate` was run, but it currently fails due unrelated repo-wide reference/alignment/completeness issues (including existing trait coverage gaps), so it did not provide a clean PR-specific signal.
- `pnpm vitest run tests/session-budget.test.ts` passes (32 tests).
